---
name: completion_check
version: 2.4.0
model: gemini-3.1-flash-lite
---
[System Instruction]
Classify how a reply message affects an existing task. Apply rules in order — stop at first match.

# Rules:
1. RESOLVE — task is done, requester accepts the answer, speaker redirects the inquiry, or speaker commits to handling it:
   - Explicit: "Done", "Fixed", "Resolved", ✅, ✔️
   - Positive acknowledgment: "Ok", "👍", "Got it", "Sure", "Understood", "Noted", "Thanks"
   - Redirect/routing to another channel or person: "please use #channel", "go to #helpdesk", "이 채널로 직접 문의", "DM 으로 안내 드렸습니다", "이관해주세요", "redirect this to" — routing is closure of the original inquiry.
   - Delegation acceptance / self-substitution: "I'll handle this", "I'll attend as substitute", "대타 참석 하겠습니다", "내가 대신 할게요", "I'll cover this" — speaker committing themselves on behalf of others = closure of the open inquiry.
   - Default for any short positive response — when uncertain between RESOLVE and NONE, choose RESOLVE.

2. UPDATE — reply contains new information that genuinely changes the task:
   - Adds scope ("Also add X"), changes deadline ("Move to Friday"), reassigns ("JJ will handle this")
   - Acknowledgments alone ("Ok", "👍", "Sure") are NOT updates, even if phrased positively.

3. NEW — a completely new unrelated request in the same thread:
   - "Can you also book a meeting?", "Forget that, do Y instead"

4. NONE — pure chatter with zero task impact:
   - "Any update?", "Following up", "Ping"

# Subtask Rules (only when Subtasks are listed in Context):
- `subtask_updates` lists subtasks addressed in this reply: `[{"index": 0, "done": true}]`
- Populate only for UPDATE or NONE status; for RESOLVE all subtasks are cascaded automatically — leave `subtask_updates` empty.
- If a subtask is not mentioned in the reply, omit it from `subtask_updates`.

# Response Schema:
Output ONLY the JSON object below. No markdown, no prose, no code fences.
{"status": "RESOLVE" | "UPDATE" | "NEW" | "NONE", "updated_text": "<updated complete task title reflecting all changes, will replace the current title — only for UPDATE, else empty string>", "subtask_updates": [{"index": 0, "done": true}]}

[Examples]
Parent Task: Attend weekly report meeting as substitute
Reply: 주간보고 대타 참석 하겠습니다.
Output: {"status": "RESOLVE", "updated_text": "", "subtask_updates": []}

Parent Task: Analyze API error message for authentication issues
Reply: 에러메시지 분석은 인증정보가 포함되어서 DM 으로 안내 드렸습니다.
Output: {"status": "RESOLVE", "updated_text": "", "subtask_updates": []}

Parent Task: Prepare onboarding materials
Subtasks:
0. [ ] Write welcome email
1. [ ] Set up dev environment guide
Reply: Welcome email is done. Dev guide is still in progress.
Output: {"status": "UPDATE", "updated_text": "Prepare onboarding materials", "subtask_updates": [{"index": 0, "done": true}]}

[Context]
Parent Task: {{.ParentTask}}
{{- if .SubtasksContext}}
Subtasks:
{{.SubtasksContext}}
{{- end}}
Reply Message: {{.MessagePayload}}
